# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Editor / IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# Environment / secrets
.env
.env.local
*.key
credentials.json

# Dependencies / build
node_modules/
dist/
build/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/

~$*

app/node_modules/

# Portable package build output (rebuild with "Build App.bat"). The
# lockfile and api_entry.spec are tracked: they are what makes it reproducible.
build-portable/

# The firm's own redacted documents and their expectations file live
# outside the repository (TRACKER_REAL_CORPUS names the folder). This is
# for the day someone drops them inside the tree anyway: redaction is a
# person's judgement, not a guarantee, and a client document in the repo
# is in every clone and every build.
real-corpus/

# Client-provided files are sensitive — never commit actual documents.
# Track only the manifest/metadata, not the files themselves.
client-files/**
!client-files/.gitkeep
!client-files/**/.gitkeep

# Accounting / working files
*.qbw
*.qbb
*.tlg

# The clients root's two trees and every file the tracker writes inside
# them (decision 176). A pass pointed at a copy of a client's folder made
# inside the checkout - to debug one household - leaves the record, the
# page, the README and what it took out of their emails there, each one
# `git add -A` away from every clone. tests/test_single_source.py names
# each from its constant.
Clients/
J Park & Associates/
_ledger.jsonl
_scan.lock
_readme.lock
_README.txt
Status Report.html
_Opened/

# Scheduled-run artifacts. Drafts quote real clients' outstanding documents
# and the page names them; the page lives in the clients root and the drafts
# beside each engagement. The run log carries counts and codes and lives in
# the tracker's data folder since decision 186; a checkout from before it
# may hold one.
runs.log
status.html
# The clients root, written once by the app (or python -m tracker.settings).
settings.json
# The store (decision 101). Since decision 186 it lives in the tracker's
# data folder, never in a checkout; a checkout from before it may still hold
# one, and it holds every client's index rows, so it must never be committed.
tracker.db
tracker.db-wal
tracker.db-shm
pass-order.json
# Decision 159 writes beside the store too, and each holds client data or
# describes this one machine: the record checkpoint (and SQLite's two side
# files), the last-pass file (and its temp name while it is replaced), the
# exports recover keeps, and a store an older version wrote, set aside -
# which holds every client's index rows like tracker.db. Until decision 186
# moves the data home out of the program's folder, these lines are what
# keeps them out of the repository.
record-heads.db
record-heads.db-*
last-pass.json
last-pass.json.*
recovered/
tracker.db.v*.old*
# Beside the store too (decision 193): the local error log, which can name
# a client's folder, its rotated copies, and the running passes' progress
# files and cancel markers.
tracker-errors.log
tracker-errors.log.*
passes/
# Decision 209's note of the last after-install run, beside the store: it
# names this machine's findings, which can name a client's folder.
after-install.json
after-install.json.*
# OCR's temporary page images during a pass (decision 137, L7). Retired by
# decision 169 - the reader writes no temporary file - but a checkout that
# ran a pass before it may still hold the folder, with a client's page in
# it, so it stays ignored.
ocr-scratch/

# Tools' own working folders (decision 137): Claude Code's worktrees and
# personal settings, and the knowledge-graph tool's output, which quotes the
# tree. The project's own agent settings are tracked (decision 186) and carry
# a deny list of the data home, the client Shared Drive and every file that
# names a client, anywhere on the machine - a guard rail, not a wall: it
# loads only in a session started in a checkout and binds only the agent's
# file tools; the wall is the separate Windows account the office's AI
# tooling runs under.
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json
# Design skills for every session on this repo (P56): Anthropic's
# frontend-design and Impeccable, both Apache 2.0.
!.claude/skills/
graphify-out/
tax-tracker.xml
reminder-draft.txt
reminder-draft.NEW.txt
reminder-draft.set-aside-*.txt
# A temp the tracker writes beside a target before renaming it
# (fsio.TEMP_SUFFIX), and the real corpus's expectations file, which names
# the firm's own documents (decision 186).
*.tmp
expectations.csv
